LSMR — upstream provenance and license notice
=============================================

This directory contains vendored source code from the LSMR sparse
least-squares solver project.

Upstream provenance
-------------------

The original LSMR implementation is by:

  David C. Fong
  Michael A. Saunders
  Systems Optimization Laboratory (SOL)
  Stanford University

Some files used by jpolyd are from the original SOL LSMR Fortran
distribution.

The reverse-communication Fortran implementation was contributed to the
LSMR project in November 2015 by:

  Nick Gould
  Jennifer Scott
  STFC Rutherford Appleton Laboratory, United Kingdom

jpolyd uses files from both the original SOL LSMR distribution and the
Gould/Scott reverse-communication distribution because the latter relies
on components from the original implementation.

Upstream project pages:

  https://web.stanford.edu/group/SOL/software/lsmr/
  https://convexoptimization.com/sol/BSDlicense.html

Licensing note
--------------

The Systems Optimization Laboratory BSD license page explicitly lists
"lsmr" among the SOL numerical software packages to which the BSD license
below applies.

The LSMR project page separately identifies the Gould/Scott
reverse-communication implementation as an LSMR contribution. The
reverse-communication download itself does not include a separate license
file or license statement.

This file therefore preserves the SOL BSD license notice together with
the provenance of both source sets. It does not purport to relicense any
upstream code. Anyone requiring independent confirmation of the licensing
of a particular upstream file should consult the original LSMR sources,
the related SPRAL distribution, or the upstream authors.

